  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L04_007_Store Function Result In A Variable",
   "display_name": "Store Function Result In A Variable",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A returned value doesn't have to be printed immediately - it can be stored in a variable and used later, just like any other computed value, including being passed straight into more arithmetic.</p>\n<pre>def square_it(a):\n    return a * a\n\ns = square_it(4)\ntotal = s + 10\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>s</code> holds the returned value (<code>16</code>), and we then use <code>s</code> in further arithmetic before printing the final result.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>square_it</code> that returns the square of its argument. Read a whole number <code>n</code>, call <code>square_it(n)</code> and store the result, then print that result <b>plus 10</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>26</pre></p>\n<p>(4 squared is 16, plus 10 is 26)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def square_it(a):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(square_it(5))",
   "mark": 1.0,
