   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L04_014_Chain Of Three Function Calls",
   "display_name": "Chain Of Three Function Calls",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Composition isn't limited to two functions - you can chain as many as you like, feeding each result into the next.</p>\n<pre>def double_it(a):\n    return a * 2\n\ndef add_ten(a):\n    return a + 10\n\ndef square_it(a):\n    return a * a\n\nx = 3\nresult = square_it(add_ten(double_it(x)))\nprint(result)</pre>\n<p><b>Trace through:</b> <code>double_it(3) = 6</code>, then <code>add_ten(6) = 16</code>, then <code>square_it(16) = 256</code>. Each function's output becomes the next function's input, working from the innermost parentheses outward.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define <code>double_it</code>, <code>add_ten</code>, and <code>square_it</code> as shown above. Read a whole number <code>x</code> and print <code>square_it(add_ten(double_it(x)))</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3</pre> Output: <pre>256</pre></p>",
