   "xml_name": "L04_017_Compare Results Of Two Functions",
   "display_name": "Compare Results Of Two Functions",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use two functions' return values together in an <code>if</code>-<code>else</code> comparison, right in the caller's code.</p>\n<pre>def square_it(a):\n    return a * a\n\ndef cube_it(a):\n    return a * a * a\n\nn = 2\nif cube_it(n) > square_it(n):\n    print(\"Cube is bigger\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Square is bigger or equal\")</pre>\n<p>Both <code>cube_it(n)</code> and <code>square_it(n)</code> are computed and compared, exactly like comparing any two values with <code>&gt;</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define <code>square_it(a)</code> and <code>cube_it(a)</code> as shown above. Read a whole number <code>n</code>. Print <code>Cube is bigger</code> if <code>cube_it(n)</code> is greater than <code>square_it(n)</code>, otherwise print <code>Square is bigger or equal</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> Input: <pre>2</pre> Output: <pre>Cube is bigger</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - equal, n=1):</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>Square is bigger or equal</pre></p>",
