   "xml_index": 18,
   "xml_name": "L04_018_Loop Calling A Function Each Iteration",
   "display_name": "Loop Calling A Function Each Iteration",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Loops and functions combine very naturally: a loop can call the same function once per iteration, with a different argument each time.</p>\n<pre>def square_it(a):\n    return a * a\n\nn = 5\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    print(square_it(i))</pre>\n<p>Each pass through the loop calls <code>square_it</code> with the current value of <code>i</code>, printing the squares of 1 through <code>n</code> one by one.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define <code>square_it(a)</code> returning <code>a squared</code>. Read a whole number <code>n</code> and, using a <code>for</code> loop, print the squares of every whole number from 1 to <code>n</code> (inclusive), each on its own line, by calling <code>square_it</code> each time.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>4</pre> Output: <pre>1\n4\n9\n16</pre></p>",
