  {
   "xml_index": 19,
   "xml_name": "L04_019_Three Step Function Pipeline",
   "display_name": "Three Step Function Pipeline",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's write three small functions that are meant to be used together in sequence, each one processing the previous step's result - a very common real-world pattern (sometimes called a \"pipeline\").</p>\n<pre>def get_discounted_price(price):\n    return price - (price * 10 / 100)\n\ndef add_tax(price):\n    return price + (price * 5 / 100)\n\ndef round_price(price):\n    return round(price, 2)\n\noriginal = 100\nfinal = round_price(add_tax(get_discounted_price(original)))\nprint(final)</pre>\n<p>Each function does one clear step: apply a discount, then add tax, then round for display. Composing them (innermost first) gives the final price in one expression.</p>\n<p><b>Reminder:</b> since these compute floats, we round the final result with <code>round(price, 2)</code>, done here inside <code>round_price</code> itself.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define <code>get_discounted_price</code>, <code>add_tax</code>, and <code>round_price</code> exactly as shown above. Read a whole number <code>original</code> price and print <code>round_price(add_tax(get_discounted_price(original)))</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>100</pre> Output: <pre>94.5</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "def get_discounted_price(price):\n    # write your code here\n\n\ndef add_tax(price):\n    # write your code here\n\n\ndef round_price(price):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your functions; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(round_price(add_tax(get_discounted_price(100))))",
