   "xml_name": "L04_022_Multiple Return Values Smaller And Larger",
   "display_name": "Multiple Return Values Smaller And Larger",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's practice multiple return values with a comparison: given two numbers, return both the smaller and larger of the two, in that order.</p>\n<pre>def order(a, b):\n    if a < b:\n        return a, b\n    else:\n        return b, a\n\nsmaller, larger = order(8, 3)\nprint(smaller)\nprint(larger)</pre>\n<p>Notice both <code>return</code> statements return a pair - just in a different order depending on which branch runs, so the caller can always rely on the first unpacked variable being the smaller one.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>order</code> that takes two parameters <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>, and returns them as <code>(smaller, larger)</code>. Read two whole numbers, call <code>order</code>, unpack the results, and print the smaller value then the larger value, each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>8\n3</pre> Output: <pre>3\n8</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case (equal values):</b> Input: <pre>5\n5</pre> Output: <pre>5\n5</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "def order(a, b):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# smaller, larger = order(8, 3)\n# print(smaller, larger)",
