   "xml_name": "L04_029_Function Taking A List Returning Count Even",
   "display_name": "Taking A List Returning Count Even",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's write a function that combines a loop, an <code>if</code>, and a counter, wrapped up so it can be reused on any list.</p>\n<pre>def count_evens(lst):\n    count = 0\n    for value in lst:\n        if value % 2 == 0:\n            count = count + 1\n    return count\n\nnumbers = [3, 8, 15, 6, 21, 4]\nprint(count_evens(numbers))</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>count_evens</code> that takes one parameter <code>lst</code> and returns how many of its elements are even, using the technique shown above. Call it with the fixed list <code>[3, 8, 15, 6, 21, 4]</code> and print the result.</p>\n<p><b>Expected Output:</b></p>\n<pre>3</pre>",
