   "xml_index": 30,
   "xml_name": "L04_030_Function Combining List And Loop Filtered Count",
   "display_name": "Combining List And Loop Filtered Count",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine a list parameter with a second, ordinary parameter - a threshold value to compare against.</p>\n<pre>def count_greater_than(lst, x):\n    count = 0\n    for value in lst:\n        if value > x:\n            count = count + 1\n    return count\n\nnumbers = [11, 4, 18, 7, 25, 2, 14]\nprint(count_greater_than(numbers, 10))</pre>\n<p>This is our last \"simple\" list question before we start mixing in some truly hidden tests for the rest of the lab - by now you've seen every building block needed: functions, parameters (including list parameters), loops, and accumulators, all working together.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>count_greater_than</code> that takes a list <code>lst</code> and a value <code>x</code>, and returns how many elements of <code>lst</code> are greater than <code>x</code>. Call it with the fixed list <code>[11, 4, 18, 7, 25, 2, 14]</code>, read a whole number <code>x</code>, and print the result.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> Input: <pre>10</pre> Output: <pre>4</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - nothing qualifies):</b> Input: <pre>100</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
