   "xml_name": "L04_031_Function With Nested Loop Printing A Square",
   "display_name": "With Nested Loop Printing A Square",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A function's body can contain a full nested loop too - here, a function that <b>prints</b> a pattern (no return value needed, since printing is itself the \"output\").</p>\n<pre>def print_square(n):\n    for row in range(n):\n        for col in range(n):\n            print(\"*\", end=\"\")\n        print()\n\nprint_square(4)</pre>\n<p>This is exactly the nested-loop square pattern from Lab 3, wrapped in a function so we can print a square of any size just by calling <code>print_square</code> with a different argument.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>print_square</code> that takes one parameter <code>n</code> and prints an <code>n</code> by <code>n</code> square of stars (no return value needed). Read a whole number and call <code>print_square</code> with it.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3</pre> Output: <pre>***\n***\n***</pre></p>",
