   "xml_name": "L04_032_Function Computing Grid Sum Using Nested Loop",
   "display_name": "Computing Grid Sum Using Nested Loop",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's write a function that <b>returns</b> a value computed by a nested loop, rather than printing a pattern - reusing the grid-sum idea from Lab 3.</p>\n<pre>def grid_sum(n):\n    total = 0\n    for row in range(1, n + 1):\n        for col in range(1, n + 1):\n            total = total + (row * col)\n    return total\n\nprint(grid_sum(3))</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>grid_sum</code> that takes one parameter <code>n</code> and returns the sum of every entry in the <code>n</code> by <code>n</code> multiplication grid (entry at row <code>r</code>, column <code>c</code> is <code>r * c</code>), using the technique shown above. Read a whole number, call <code>grid_sum</code>, and print the result.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3</pre> Output: <pre>36</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define a function named grid_sum that takes one int parameter: n\n# It should return the sum of every entry in the n by n multiplication grid\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(grid_sum(3))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
