  {
   "xml_index": 33,
   "xml_name": "L04_033_Loop Calling Function To Accumulate",
   "display_name": "Loop Calling Function To Accumulate",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine a loop-calling-a-function pattern (like question 18) with an accumulator, to sum up the results of many function calls.</p>\n<pre>def square_it(a):\n    return a * a\n\ndef sum_of_squares_upto(n):\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        total = total + square_it(i)\n    return total\n\nprint(sum_of_squares_upto(3))</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>sum_of_squares_upto</code> is itself a function, and its body calls <code>square_it</code> once per loop iteration, adding each result into a running total - combining composition, loops, and accumulators all in one.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define <code>square_it(a)</code> returning <code>a squared</code>, and <code>sum_of_squares_upto(n)</code> which uses a <code>for</code> loop calling <code>square_it</code> to compute the sum of squares from 1 to <code>n</code>. Read a whole number, call <code>sum_of_squares_upto</code>, and print the result.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3</pre> Output: <pre>14</pre></p>\n<p><b>Edge case:</b> Input: <pre>1</pre> Output: <pre>1</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define a function named square_it that takes one int parameter: a (returns a squared)\n# Define a function named sum_of_squares_upto that takes one int parameter: n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your functions; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(sum_of_squares_upto(3))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
