   "xml_index": 34,
   "xml_name": "L04_034_Loop With Multiple Return Values",
   "display_name": "Loop With Multiple Return Values",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's call a multiple-return function repeatedly inside a loop, unpacking fresh results on every pass.</p>\n<pre>def divide(a, b):\n    return a // b, a % b\n\nn = 3\nfor i in range(n):\n    a = int(input())\n    b = int(input())\n    q, r = divide(a, b)\n    print(q, r)</pre>\n<p>Each pass through the loop reads a new pair of numbers, calls <code>divide</code>, unpacks the two results into <code>q</code> and <code>r</code>, and prints them - the unpacking works exactly the same way inside a loop as it does outside one.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a function named <code>divide</code> that returns the quotient and remainder of <code>a // b</code> and <code>a % b</code>. Read a whole number <code>n</code>, then read <code>n</code> pairs of whole numbers (two per pair, one per line). For each pair, call <code>divide</code>, unpack the results, and print them space-separated on one line (quotient then remainder).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>2\n17\n5\n9\n3</pre> Output: <pre>3 2\n3 0</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define a function named divide that takes two int parameters: a, b\n# It should return two values: the quotient (a // b) and the remainder (a % b)\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# q, r = divide(17, 5)\n# print(q, r)",
